{
  "question_id": "q_020_non_profitable_drugs",
  "slug": "non-profitable-drugs",
  "title": "Pharmacy Analytics (Part 2)",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "company": "CVS Health",
  "premium": false,
  "question": "CVS Health pharmacy financial auditors analyze prescription drug profitability across pharmaceutical manufacturers.\n\nFor drugs where production cost of goods sold (`cogs`) exceeded `total_sales`, the drug operated at a loss.\n\nWrite a query to find the total loss and count of unprofitable drugs for each manufacturer. Output the `manufacturer`, `drug_count` (unprofitable drugs only), and `total_loss` (sum of `cogs - total_sales`). Sort by `total_loss` in descending order.",
  "notes": [
    "The first three rows indicate that some drugs resulted in losses. Among these, Biogen had the highest losses, followed by AbbVie and Eli Lilly. However, the Medi-Chord drug manufactured by Biogen reported a profit and was excluded from the result."
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "pharmacy_sales",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "product_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "units_sold",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "total_sales",
          "data_type": "DECIMAL(10,2)"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "cogs",
          "data_type": "DECIMAL(10,2)"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "manufacturer",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(255)"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "drug",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(255)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sample_data": {
    "pharmacy_sales": [
      {
        "product_id": "156",
        "units_sold": "89514",
        "total_sales": "3130097.00",
        "cogs": "3427421.73",
        "manufacturer": "Biogen",
        "drug": "Acyclovir"
      },
      {
